course: dictionary
lesson: 10049
title: Territorial
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Territorial means about an area that belongs to a country, an animal or a person. When you meet it, look at the words around it to find the area. «Countries also have borders at sea, with territorial waters reaching 12 nautical miles from the coast.» The sea next to a country belongs to that country, so territorial waters must be the sea near its coast.
explain: The word can also describe animals. «Hippos yawn widely to show their huge teeth as a warning; they are very territorial» tells you hippos warn others to keep away. A territorial animal guards its own patch and chases others out. Robins and cats do this too.
explain: The word can describe people. «That's the Year 6 table, they're well territorial» means the older children guard their table and do not want others to sit there. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "they're well guarding their space" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Territorial means about an area of land or sea that belongs to someone or something.
fact: «Territorial waters» are the sea near a country's coast that belongs to that country.
fact: A nautical mile is a sea mile, a bit under 2 kilometres, so 12 nautical miles is about 22 kilometres.
fact: A territorial animal defends its own patch and chases others away from it.
fact: «Territorial disputes» are arguments between countries about who owns land.
exercise: «Countries also have borders at sea, with territorial waters reaching 12 nautical miles from the coast.» What are territorial waters? | *The sea near a country's coast that belongs to it | A swimming pool at school | Deep water far from any land | A kind of fish that lives near the coast
exercise: «Hippos yawn widely to show their huge teeth as a warning; they are very territorial.» What does territorial suggest about hippos? | *They guard their own area and chase others away | They like to sleep in trees | They love meeting new animals
exercise: «That's the Year 6 table, they're well territorial.» What does territorial mean here? | They like geography lessons | *They guard their space and do not want others sitting there | They are good at maps | They are happy for everyone to share
test: What is a territorial dog? | A dog that sleeps all day | A dog that swims in the sea | A dog that likes every other dog | *A dog that guards its own area and chases others away
test: What are «territorial disputes»? | Lessons about animals | *Arguments between countries about land | Arguments between countries about who owns land | Games played at break time
exam: In «Hippos are very territorial», what does territorial mean? | Good at swimming | Likes to sleep a lot | *Defends its own area and chases others away | Happy to share their home
